{"event": {"background_tasks": [], "cwd": "<scratch>/repo", "effort": {"level": "high"}, "hook_event_name": "Stop", "last_assistant_message": "Two of the eight steps were blocked: the aidd validate call (step 5) and the `file:` page in the browser (step 8). Every other step went through.\n\n| # | Step | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Read README.md | **Done.** It contains `# Scratch` / `A repository for a live hook check.` |\n| 2 | Create `notes/one.md` with \"one\" | **Done.** The aidd hook added a note but didn't block the write: \"aidd: `agents.delegate: auto` (a note, not a denial): no aidd-team role's area holds notes/one.md, so there is no role to hand it to. This session may edit it. This note comes once per session and role.\" |\n| 3 | Edit it to \"one, edited\" | **Done.** No hook note. |\n| 4 | Subagent creates `notes/two.md` with \"two\" | **Done**, per the subagent's report. The hook warned but let the write through: \"aidd (advisory mode, so this goes through): notes/two.md: a subagent that is not an aidd-team role may only read (the loop contract's helper rule, \"Use AI as a delivery team does\"). Hand the edit back to the role or the lead that started you: a role writes in its area, and only the lead starts another role (`aidd-team:<role>` in Claude Code, `aidd-<role>` in Codex, OpenCode, Grok Build, and Antigravity) This note comes once a session; later edits like it go through without one.\" |\n| 5 | aidd MCP `validate` | **Denied** by the permission system, not by an aidd hook: \"Claude requested permissions to use mcp__aidd__validate, but you haven't granted it yet.\" |\n| 6 | `git status --short` | **Done.** Output: `?? notes/` |\n| 7 | aidd-developer subagent reads README.md five times | **Done.** It made five separate Read calls and said \"done\". Only the first returned the file. Reads 2\u20135 returned \"Wasted call \u2014 file unchanged since your last Read. Refer to that earlier tool_result instead.\" The hooks added two turn-budget notes: \"aidd: you have used about 4 of your 5 turns. Finish the step you are on, then write your handoff note and report what is left.\" and \"aidd: about 0 turns are left. Finish here: write your handoff note and report what is left.\" |\n| 8a | Playwright to the `file:///\u2026/README.md` URL | **Blocked** by Playwright itself, not by a hook: \"Error: Access to \"file:\" protocol is blocked. Attempted URL: \"file://<scratch>/repo/README.md\"\" |\n| 8b | Playwright to `https://example.com` | **Done.** The page loaded with the title \"Example Domain\". The hook warned but let it through: \"aidd (advisory mode, so this goes through): the browser tool browser_navigate would open `https://example.com`, the host `example.com`, which is not a local page and not in `agents.browser_hosts`. The guard holds a browser to local pages: open a local preview (a `file:` page, or `http://localhost:<port>`, or a `*.localhost` or `*.test` host), or ask the person to add the host to `agents.browser_hosts` in .aidd/config.yaml\" |\n\nThe aidd hooks are running in advisory mode: they never blocked anything, even when they warned. The only blocks came from the permission system and from Playwright's `file:` rule. That `file:` rule also means a local `file:` preview, which the aidd hook recommends, won't open in this browser.\n\nPlaywright saved its page snapshot under a relative `.playwright-mcp/` path, so it may have created that folder inside the repo. Step 6 ran before step 8, so its output doesn't show it.", "permission_mode": "acceptEdits", "prompt_id": "4cbf1e39-e7dd-435c-a04c-7ddc5ac1cb4b", "session_crons": [], "session_id": "21b461d8-1cdc-4a74-bb2c-181a1c8a6e43", "stop_hook_active": false, "transcript_path": "~/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-d7-31s09-wx1pgf087794jsh67c0000gn-T-aidd-live-hooks-z-1ngmoa-repo/21b461d8-1cdc-4a74-bb2c-181a1c8a6e43.jsonl"}, "hook": "stop"}
